        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The most useful shower features depend on the person, the bathroom, mobility, bathing preferences, and whether assistance is needed. The commonly considered set: a low or curbless entrance, properly anchored grab bars, stable seating, a handheld showerhead, reachable controls, slip-resistant surfaces, adequate lighting, predictable temperature controls, sufficient entry and maneuvering space, and effective drainage. No individual feature makes a shower universally safe or accessible — features work as a set, chosen for the specific user."
